# Welcome from the Family

## A Life Remembered

### English

**Welcome to the remembrance of our beloved husband, father, brother, and friend, Sri Kanagala Balarama Krishna.**

With love and gratitude, we have created this space to remember and celebrate a life that meant so much to us and to the many people whose lives he touched.

For our family, he was the person at the heart of our home—the one who worked tirelessly for us, carried his responsibilities with dedication, and filled our lives with countless moments that we will cherish forever. To those who knew him beyond our family, he was a trusted friend, a familiar face, and someone they could approach with warmth and confidence.

This is not simply a collection of photographs or a record of dates and events.

It is a place where **his story lives**.

Here, we have brought together memories from the different chapters of his life—his childhood and early years, his dreams and aspirations, his work, his family, the relationships he built, the simple things he loved, and the final chapter of his journey.

We have also preserved the story of his final act of selflessness—his decision, through our family, to donate his organs and eyes so that others could have the opportunity to live and see.

As you move through these pages, we invite you to discover not only **how he lived**, but also **the kind of person he was**.

Some memories may bring a smile.

Some may bring tears.

And some may simply make you pause and remember.

Whatever you feel, we hope you will carry one thing with you when you leave this space:

**A little more of the man we were blessed to call ours.**

With love,
**The Family of
Sri Kanagala Balarama Krishna**

